---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  The top app bar provides content and actions related to the current screen. Use the
  <code>start</code> slot for a navigation icon, the default slot for the headline, and the
  <code>end</code> slot for action icon buttons.
</p>
<p>
  The app bar is not a landmark, so it fits in cards, panes and dialogs without adding extra
  banners. When it is the page's header, wrap it in a <code>&lt;header&gt;</code> element to make
  it the banner landmark.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <div style='width: 100%; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 0.5rem;'>
    <header>
      <wc-app-bar>
        <wc-icon-button slot='start' variant='text' aria-label='Menu'>
          <wc-icon name='menu'></wc-icon>
        </wc-icon-button>
        Page Title
        <wc-icon-button slot='end' variant='text' aria-label='Search'>
          <wc-icon name='search'></wc-icon>
        </wc-icon-button>
        <wc-icon-button slot='end' variant='text' aria-label='More'>
          <wc-icon name='more_vert'></wc-icon>
        </wc-icon-button>
      </wc-app-bar>
    </header>
  </div>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>Deprecated</h3>
<ul>
  <li>
    The <code>leading</code> and <code>trailing</code> slots: use <code>start</code> and
    <code>end</code>. They still work and log a warning; they are removed in 4.0.
  </li>
  <li>
    The app bar no longer sets <code>role="banner"</code> on itself. Put it in a
    <code>&lt;header&gt;</code> where it is the page banner.
  </li>
</ul>
